// .mdix/replacements/replacements.mdix
//
// This drop fixes the CI break the previous drop
// (msx-image-audio-COMPLETE-DROP.tar.gz) introduced, and finishes the
// msx-render-gpu Image wiring the handover after that left incomplete.
//
// ROOT CAUSE of the CI break: this file used to carry a blanket
//   overrides::
//     target("Cargo.toml", "./Cargo.toml")
// which forces ANY file named "Cargo.toml" anywhere in an applied
// tarball to land at the workspace ROOT, regardless of its real nested
// path inside the tarball. When the image/audio drop included
// render/msx-render-svg/Cargo.toml (to add its new `base64` dep), that
// override redirected it on top of the real workspace-root Cargo.toml
// instead — clobbering `[workspace]`/`[workspace.dependencies]`
// entirely. The root Cargo.toml was manually reconstructed afterward,
// but the `base64` dependency it had accidentally picked up got dropped
// in that reconstruction rather than routed to where it actually
// belonged, and the equivalent `image` dependency for
// msx-render-cpu/msx-render-gpu was never added at all — hence
// msx-parser failing CI with "cannot find crate `base64`".
//
// THE FIX, going forward: that override is gone. A bare basename
// override like `target("Cargo.toml", ...)` is dangerous in THIS repo
// specifically because there are 13 different Cargo.toml files in the
// tree (root + one per crate) — the override-matching check runs BEFORE
// nested-path resolution and matches on bare basename, so it silently
// catches every one of them, not just the one it was written for.
// Nested paths already resolve correctly on their own (direct,
// target_root-relative, no search, no ambiguity) — that's why removing
// the override outright is the fix, not narrowing it.
//
// The ONE file in this drop that's genuinely at the repo root (the
// workspace Cargo.toml itself) is shipped inside the archive as
// `ROOT_Cargo.toml` — a name no other file in this repo's tree could
// ever collide with — and mapped via an explicit override below. This
// is the documented mdix-scaffold pattern for exactly this situation
// (see MDIX_SCAFFOLD_SKILL.md's "Gotcha, found the hard way"): don't
// override a shared basename, rename the flat file to something
// globally unique and override THAT.
//
// Everything else in this drop sits inside the archive at its real
// nested subdirectory path (core/msx-parser/Cargo.toml,
// render/msx-render-svg/Cargo.toml, render/msx-render-cpu/Cargo.toml,
// render/msx-render-gpu/Cargo.toml, render/msx-render-gpu/src/lib.rs,
// render/msx-render-gpu/src/layer.rs) — resolved directly by path, never
// touches the override, never searches.
//
// What this drop's file contents actually do:
//   - adds the missing `base64` workspace dependency (msx-parser,
//     msx-render-svg) and `image` workspace dependency (msx-render-cpu,
//     msx-render-gpu) that their own source already required
//   - pins `image` to `=0.25.0` with `default-features = false,
//     features = ["png", "jpeg"]` in the root workspace manifest — a
//     bare `image = "0.25"` (even individually re-pinned via
//     `cargo update --precise`) still resolves a default-feature build
//     that pulls in the avif encoder path (ravif -> rav1e ->
//     avif-serialize), and avif-serialize needs Cargo's edition2024
//     support, unavailable at this workspace's capped rustc/cargo 1.75.
//     Restricting features at the Cargo.toml level avoids that chain
//     ever being resolved in the first place. Confirmed via a real,
//     from-scratch `cargo test` in an isolated workspace at rustc 1.75.
//   - finishes msx-render-gpu's Image wiring: `mod image;` was never
//     declared in lib.rs even though layer.rs's `draw_run` already
//     referenced `crate::image::ImagePipeline` (an existing,
//     compile-blocking gap independent of the dependency issue above);
//     `GpuRenderer` now constructs and stores an `ImagePipeline` and
//     threads it through `render_ordered`'s signature, its call to
//     `draw_run`, and BOTH of its calls to `LayerCompositor::render_layer`
//     (the sibling-scoped `Composite` arm AND the Group-nested-layers
//     leftover loop — the previous handover's fix plan only accounted
//     for one of these two call sites)

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  author     -> "MidManStudio"

  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@QUICKFUNCS(
  ~target<object>(name, path) { return { name = name, path = path } }
)

@DATA(
  target_root = "."

  overrides::
    target("ROOT_Cargo.toml", "./Cargo.toml")
)
